{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1518004-the-course-of-history-with-multiple-allegiances-devoted-to-advancing-social-issues","id":1518004,"title":"The course of history with multiple Allegiances devoted to advancing social issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-14T23:11:22-07:00","id":1518004,"title":"The course of history with multiple Allegiances devoted to advancing social issues","content":"The old World of Darkness had an issue with the course of history being defined by a small number of supernatural groups and individuals. The Trinity Continuum seems to suffer something similar with so many Inspired groups being devoted to fighting for societal change. This has some problematic aspects when it comes to the agency of normal people. How is this resolved?<br /> <br /> Alright, first it seems like positive change primarily happened because of Inspired individuals. That's pretty fatalistic when it comes to humanities ability to improve itself. If humanity is responsible for the improvement then that implies that the inspired were just spinning their wheels. They essentially failed in their efforts. Not great for empowering players and making them think their efforts matter.<br /> <br /> Is the &quot;current year&quot; of the core book era perhaps better off then our own world? Is that a way to reconcile this issue? Or perhaps the Allegiances of the past were so busy fighting inspired villains that the positive changes they <i>were</i> responsible for were balanced out by the negative effects of the villains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T03:15:21-07:00","id":1518139,"title":"","content":"It's entirely my possible to say that there was no <b>Adventure!</b> or <b>Aether</b> in the history of the core book's modern era; it's in a part of the Continuum untouched by those events. It's <i>definitely</i> in a part of the Continuum where <b>Aberrant</b> never happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T19:02:58-07:00","id":1518161,"title":"","content":"What? Sure, the individual gm has the right to say what is and isn't canon for their game. And it is a sure thing that if you are playing a game earlier in the timeline pc actions will throw the plot off the rails for the events later in the timeline. However, I figured the baseline assumption is that if you are playing, say, Aberrant then the Corebook and Adventure eras played out in a specific, canonical, way. Doctor Primaris becomes Divis Mal, Project Utopia gets started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T21:31:06-07:00","id":1518166,"title":"","content":"The core book's setting is set in the current year: that was 2019 when the book was published, and his now 2023. According to TC: Aberrant (published in 2020), N-Day was March 23, 2018. That is, when it was published, N-Day was <i>already</i> two years in the past; and even when the core book was published, N-Day was already a year in the past. <br /> <br /> TC:Aberrant has <i>never</i> been the future of the core book's setting. The core book's setting has always existed \u201coff to the side\u201d of the timeline running from Aether through Adventure!, Aberrant, and Anima and up to \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> I'll retract my suggestion that TC:Adventure! never happened in the core setting, as the \u00c6on Society in the core book and its history clearly indicates that it did. But at some point, it branched off and became its own timeline. Perhaps the divergence point was that Dr. Primorius never became Divas Mal: either he was killed somewhere along the way, or Max managed to talk him down from his proto-Teragen leanings. Or perhaps the future has merely been delayed, and this timeline's version of N-Day is mere days in the future. <br /> <br /> That said, TC: Adventure! has a Fate of Humanity called \u201cMutually Assured Destruction\u201d that speculates on what would happen if Mercer, Primorius, and Sara were to die early on; and part of that speculation is that instead of Primorius becoming Divas Mal and ushering in the Nova Age, Talents would develop further, into people who can consciously control probabilities. It's possible that TC:Assassins is the early stages of that sort of ability, with its Masteries that are capable of doing impossible things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T01:32:44-07:00","id":1518171,"title":"","content":"As to example <i>'<b>Core </b>setting without <b>Aberrant</b>'</i> - I point you to <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1468693-tc-assasins-instead-aberrant-on-timeline?p=1498622#post1498622\">my fan timeline that branches on Core's 2018 in that 'it's our world till 2025'</a> </b>( Well, <b>Aberrant</b> era is more delayed by 2 decades from official line in it. And <b>Assassins</b> are prominent in that take to the <b>Core</b> setting. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T09:45:59-07:00","id":1518175,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I wonder if Adventure! still took place in the past of the Corebook setting? I mean there are references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T10:21:03-07:00","id":1518185,"title":"","content":"The trinity continuum world is better than ours in small, subtle ways thanks in no small part to the efforts of the AEON society. In my headcannon, as a time traveler Max Mercer understood that true positive societal change is achieved through the combined effort of hundreds or thousands of small positive acts over a long period of time. Ordinary people can reach utopia on their own with just a bit of ordinary help, patience, and hope. Max always saw the role of extraordinary individuals as deterrents to extraordinary problems, if you start solving ordinary problems just because you're extraordinary you're taking away ordinary's people agency and their belief that they can make the world a better place, and that's without going into what happens when others don't agree with your solutions. That's why Max always worked to promote the efforts of ordinary organizations and citizens through AEON as much as possible while trying to stop the most radical actions of the extraordinary, something in which he ultimately succeeded. However, this is just my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:53:55-07:00","id":1518232,"title":"","content":"The way Core is described and the examples of tech shown in the book, even if in illustrations only, can put Core somewhere between the 1980s to 2010s, and so Core can be the past of Aberrant. It\u2019s timeless, it\u2019s just there whenever you want it to be. I mean, you can have the same technology as today, make it a 2000s SpecOp or a 80s GIJoe.<br /> <br /> To start, Core is not a setting per se, but a backdrop of all the settings, like a setting to set the settings. Basically you can always be the Talent doing talenty things in a talentish way, be it before or after N-Day (as Aberrant is the closest setting to our current time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-18-2023, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T08:26:42-07:00","id":1518243,"title":"","content":"In my head canon I see the present of the core setting as 2016, two years before N Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:32:28-07:00","id":1518256,"title":"","content":"I guess if you wanted to use the Corebook setting in the main timeline you could use a floating timeline. Aberrant is always around 10 years from now. Just treat the situation as such that behind the scenes in an modern era game the events that would have begun the Nova age went off the rails.<br /> <br /> Or a cool game might be playing through the opening years of the Nova age. Have Talents think Nova's are the usual Flux weirdness only for them to be revealed as the new normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}